  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A sudden rise in sanctions intensity restricts imports of critical goods and intermediate inputs, causing abrupt supply-side price shocks that push realized inflation above prevailing market forecasts.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">brics_global_realignment</data>
  <data key="d39">bond_inflation_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="brics_global_realignment::sanctions_intensity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::model_dev_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher sanctions intensity that restricts exports of specialized chips, cloud services, and cross‑border research collaborations directly reduces available compute, toolchains, and external partnerships, slowing the pace of designing, training and releasing new large AI models.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">brics_global_realignment</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
