<edge source="brics_global_realignment::alternative_payment_link" target="bond_inflation_shock::crossborder_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Faster integration of alternative payment rails fragments global settlement corridors and increases frictions for traditional investors and custodians, reducing net cross-border portfolio and bond flows into conventional markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">brics_global_realignment</data>
  <data key="d39">bond_inflation_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="brics_global_realignment::alternative_payment_link" target="russia_ukraine_war::shipping_transit_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Integration of alternative cross-border payment rails lowers transaction frictions for buyers and shippers excluded from mainstream finance, restoring commercial contracts and thereby increasing chartering and transit flows through maritime chokepoints once payment clearing is operational.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">brics_global_realignment</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="brics_global_realignment::alternative_payment_link" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::infra_invest_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater integration of alternative payment and settlement systems lowers cross‑border transaction frictions and counterparty risk for BRICS and allied investors, enabling faster and larger capital deployment into physical and cloud AI infrastructure in participating jurisdictions.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">brics_global_realignment</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
