</edge>
<edge source="brics_global_realignment::sanctions_evasion_capaci" target="russia_ukraine_war::fuel_supply_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Expanded sanctions-evasion networks (front companies, reflagging, shadow brokers) enable sanctioned fuel cargoes to be rechartered, transshipped and insured through third-party intermediaries, increasing actual fuel shipments through regional routes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">brics_global_realignment</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="brics_global_realignment::sanctions_evasion_capaci" target="russia_ukraine_war::grain_export_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved evasion capacity allows agricultural exporters to use middlemen, opaque paperwork and re-routing via permissive ports, raising the volume of grain shipments reaching international buyers despite formal restrictions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">brics_global_realignment</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="brics_global_realignment::sanctions_evasion_capaci" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::semiconductor_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved sanctions‑evasion capacity—via procurement intermediaries, gray‑market logistics and substitute supply chains—allows sanctioned fabs and buyers to obtain critical equipment and inputs, permitting maintenance or incremental expansion of semiconductor production capacity despite formal controls.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">brics_global_realignment</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="brics_global_realignment::sanctions_evasion_capaci" target="us_iran_maritime_standof::chokepoint_throughput" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved BRICS-enabled sanctions‑evasion networks (shadow shipping services, ship-to-ship transfers, and opaque brokerage) allow more Iranian crude to reach buyers, directly increasing volumes transiting strategic chokepoints such as the Strait of Hormuz.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">brics_global_realignment</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_maritime_standof</data>
</edge>
